      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch on the cached `\u003cgr-diff-view\u003e` behavior when navigating `Up` and back after closing chat!\n\nRather than calling `updatePreferences({ diff_page_sidebar: \u0027NONE\u0027 })` when opening chat, I guarded `connectedCallback()`\u0027s `preferences$` hydration with a one-time per-instance flag so `\u003cgr-diff-view\u003e` only initializes `shownSidebar` from `diff_page_sidebar` on initial creation for a CL, not on cached view reconnects.\n\nTwo reasons for preferring that over mutating `diff_page_sidebar`:\n1. **Preserves user defaults for ephemeral chat usage**: `diff_page_sidebar` is persisted on the server (`PUT /accounts/self/preferences`), whereas Agent Chat is currently per-CL/ephemeral in `ChatModel` (resetting on change switches, matching `gr-change-view`). If a user has a sidebar like AI Rationale pinned by default and clicks `\"Explain this code\"` or opens chat on one diff, overwriting `diff_page_sidebar` to `\u0027NONE\u0027` would permanently disable their pinned sidebar across all future CLs.\n2. **Covers opening chat from Change View first**: If a user opens `\"Agent Chat\"` on Change View before entering Diff View, `this.shownSidebar` wasn\u0027t set to the plugin sidebar when `chatPanelOpen$` fired, so checking `this.shownSidebar` wouldn\u0027t clear `diff_page_sidebar` anyway—and closing chat + re-entering cached Diff View would still hit the same reopen bug. Guarding `connectedCallback()` handles both entry points cleanly.\n\n(Persisting Agent Chat\u0027s own open state across CLs would be a broader `ChatModel` + `gr-change-view` change since `ChatModel` currently resets `chatPanelOpen` on every change switch, so keeping `diff_page_sidebar` scoped to plugin sidebars feels right here—let me know what you think!)",
